  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef sells sandwiches for a living. Each sandwich is sold for AAA rupees.\n\nChef also needs to buy the ingredients to make a sandwich. The sandwich buns cost BBB rupees, and the vegetables cost CCC rupees. Let us assume that there are no other costs for Chef right now.\n\nWhat is the profit Chef makes in selling one sandwich? It may be possible that the answer is negative to indicate that Chef makes a loss instead.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains 333 integers - A,BA, BA,B and CCC.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the profit or loss Chef makes in selling one sandwich.",
    "constraints": [
      "100≤A≤1000100 \\le A \\le 1000100≤A≤1000",
      "40≤B≤20040 \\le B \\le 20040≤B≤200",
      "40≤C≤20040 \\le C \\le 20040≤C≤200"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1000 200 200",
        "output": "600",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef needs 400400400 rupees to buy all the ingredients, and then sells it for 100010001000 rupees, so he makes a profit of 600600600 rupees."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "100 200 200",
        "output": "-300",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef needs 400400400 rupees to buy all the ingredients, and then sells it for 100100100 rupees, so he makes a loss of 300300300 rupees."
      }
    ]
  },
